    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling offensive output today, anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) and **Trea Turner** (78.64). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** earns the top spot in our lineup, benefiting from a combination of elite sprint speed\u2014our primary target for stolen base scarcity\u2014and a favorable matchup against Michael Lorenzen. His efficiency is bolstered by a 14% boost from a hitter-friendly park and a +10% lift from the leadoff spot. Similarly, **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** (77.46) are primed to exploit Max Scherzer\u2019s vulnerability against the current rotation. Both players are seeing massive +19% bumps due to the projected inefficiency of the opposing starter, and their high-leverage positions in the batting order make them the primary engines of our 5x5 Roto scoring for the day.\n\nWhile our core is strong, we are closely monitoring the 41% rain risk surrounding **Carson Benge** (61.51). Despite the weather warning, his projection remains solid due to the platoon advantage against Andre Pallante. The most difficult decision at the margins was the exclusion of **Lars Nootbaar** (48.90). While **Lars Nootbaar** posted a respectable score\u2014aided by a high xwOBA\u2014he was edged out by the superior plate discipline and positional leverage of **Christian Yelich** and **Luke Raley**, the latter of whom benefits from a significant 16% park factor boost. We remain cautious with our utility slot; if the weather report worsens for **Carson Benge**, we have the depth to pivot, though we are currently comfortable riding the high-upside matchup against the middle-of-the-road pitching staff on tap.",
